        <briefdescription>
<para>Safely determines the size of a range. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This function returns the size of a range if it is a sized range, otherwise it computes the distance between the beginning and end of the range. Note that computing the distance for non-sized ranges may be expensive.</para>
<para><blockquote><para><zwj/>[!WARNING] This function will consume input ranges that are not sized, as it needs to iterate through them to count the elements. </para>
</blockquote><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>R</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the range. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>r</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The range to measure. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The size of the range if it is a sized range, otherwise the distance between the beginning and end of the range.</para>
</simplesect>
<blockquote><para><zwj/>[!INFO] Time Complexity</para>
<para><ref refid="group__GL-Core_1gaaae078e2ee09bb6b088baac9cb8f23c9" kindref="member">$O(1)</ref>$ if the range is a sized range, otherwise <ref refid="group__GL-Core_1gaaae078e2ee09bb6b088baac9cb8f23c9" kindref="member">$O(N)</ref>$ where $N$ is the number of elements in the range. </para>
</blockquote></para>
        </detaileddescription>
